[2026-09-21 15:12:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109] verdict: The CometEls census dipole (n=268, d_par=+0.105) survives the discovery-footprint null -- preserving each aphelion's ecliptic latitude while isotropizing ecliptic longitude (p=0.0017) as it did the galactic-tide null (p=0.00195).  Under magnitude terciles, era terciles, and perihelion-distance terciles the lean stays positive in 9/9 bins, and a single common amplitude is consistent with every variable's partition (H p=0.921, era p=0.917, q p=0.545) -- the dipole is a population property, not a brightness, epoch, or perihelion-selection artefact.
